/godot/pull/123477.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-16T16:22:29Z"},"body":"Closes #123386\n\n#### Changes made\n\n- Documented on `AcceptDialog.get_ok_button()`, `AcceptDialog.add_button()`, `AcceptDialog.add_cancel_button()`, and `ConfirmationDialog.get_cancel_button()` that setting `Control.custom_minimum_size` on the returned button has no effect, and pointed to the `buttons_min_width` and `buttons_min_height` theme constants instead.\n- Documented on both theme constants that the dialog applies them to every button in the bottom row, overwriting the buttons' own `custom_minimum_size`.\n\n`AcceptDialog::_update_child_rects()` (`scene/gui/dialogs.cpp`) assigns `Size2(theme_cache.buttons_min_width, theme_cache.buttons_min_height)` to each button in the bottom row, and runs on visibility, size, theme, and button list changes, so any `custom_minimum_size` set by the user is reset. As noted in the issue this is intended behavior, so this PR only documents it.\n\nValidated with `misc/scripts/validate_xml.py` and `doc/tools/make_rst.py`, and checked the generated reStructuredText to confirm all `[member]` and `[theme_item]` references resolve, including the cross-class ones in `ConfirmationDialog`.\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/p